  "documented_gene_level_owed_disorders": {
    "PTSD": "PGC-PTSD (Nievergelt 2019; Stein 2021): few genome-wide loci, gene resolution emerging; OWED.",
    "_what": "Disorders whose GWAS architecture is real but NOT yet resolved to high-confidence INDIVIDUAL causal genes (effect sizes tiny, loci span many genes). Per the user directive 'not 100% physically, as much as possible' and the no-tuning rule, fetching weak/ambiguous candidates would be over-claiming, so these are DOCUMENTED as roadmap-covered with gene-level resolution OWED to future fine-mapping -- NOT filled with low-confidence picks.",
    "anxiety_disorders": "Largely polygenic; loci overlap MDD; few gene-level high-confidence assignments (Purves 2020). Shares the verified MDD set; standalone genes OWED.",
    "eating_disorders": "Anorexia (Watson 2019 Nat Genet): metabolic + psychiatric loci, not gene-resolved at high confidence; OWED.",
    "personality_disorders": "Heterogeneous, sparse molecular genetics; OWED."
  },
